---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
const submissionUrl = "https://github.com/hara-lang/hara-world/issues/new?template=source-submission.yml";
---
<SiteLayout title="Submit a source" description="Register an RSS or Atom publication for inclusion in Hara World.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">World Feed / source registry</p>
      <h1>Bring your own publication.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Submit an RSS or Atom feed you own or are authorised to represent. Hara World will review provenance, relevance, and syndication permission before ingestion.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href={submissionUrl}>Open a source submission <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/hara-lang/hara-world/blob/main/EDITORIAL.md">Read the editorial policy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Submission contract</p><h2>Four things we need to know.</h2></div>
        <p>These fields are kept in the source registry so that automation never has to guess whether it may republish someone’s work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="release-flow">
        <article><h3>Identity</h3><p>Publication name, homepage, feed URL, author or organisation, and a contact path.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Relevance</h3><p>How the publication relates to Hara, Lisp, language tools, runtime systems, or programmable media.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Permission</h3><p>Whether Hara World may link only, carry an excerpt, or republish full text under a stated licence.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Topics</h3><p>A small stable set of tags used for feeds, digests, and future channel-specific lists.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Revocation</h3><p>A person who can request pause, correction, or removal if the publication changes hands or policy.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="callout">
        <p class="eyebrow">Default mode</p>
        <h2>Excerpt, attribution, canonical link.</h2>
        <p>Hara World does not scrape and re-host full articles merely because a feed exposes content. Full-text syndication is opt-in; excerpt syndication remains reversible and sends readers to the original publication.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
